@startuml London TDD Workflow with Weaver

!define RED_COLOR #E74C3C
!define GREEN_COLOR #2ECC71
!define BLUE_COLOR #3498DB

title London TDD Workflow (Mock-Driven Development with Weaver Validation)

participant "Developer" as Dev
participant "Schema Registry" as Schema
participant "Weaver Generate" as Weaver
participant "Mock Generator" as MockGen
participant "Test Suite" as Tests
participant "Implementation" as Impl
participant "Live-Check" as LiveCheck

== Phase 1: Schema-First (Interface Definition) ==

Dev -> Schema : 1. Define telemetry schema
activate Schema
note right
  span.container_execution:
    attributes:
      - container.id: string, required
      - container.image: string, required
      - container.state: enum, required
      - exit_code: int, optional
end note

Dev -> Weaver : 2. weaver registry check
Weaver -> Schema : validate schema
Weaver --> Dev : ✓ schema valid

Dev -> Weaver : 3. weaver registry generate rust
Weaver -> Schema : load schema
Weaver --> Dev : generated builders

Dev -> Weaver : 4. weaver registry generate mocks
Weaver -> Schema : load schema
Weaver --> MockGen : generate mock traits
deactivate Schema

note right of MockGen #BLUE_COLOR
  Generated Mock:

  trait ContainerExecutionSpan {
    fn set_container_id(&self, id: &str);
    fn set_image(&self, image: &str);
    fn set_state(&self, state: ContainerState);
    fn set_exit_code(&self, code: i32);
  }

  Mock validates schema contract
end note

== Phase 2: Red - Write Failing Tests (London TDD) ==

Dev -> Tests : 5. Write test with mocks
activate Tests
note right #RED_COLOR
  #[test]
  fn test_container_execution_exports_telemetry() {
    // Arrange - Mock based on schema
    let mock_span = MockContainerExecutionSpan::new();
    mock_span.expect_set_container_id()
      .with(eq("test-123"))
      .times(1)
      .return_const(());

    // Act
    let result = execute_container("alpine", mock_span);

    // Assert
    assert!(result.is_ok());
    // Mock verifies schema contract called
  }
end note

Dev -> Tests : run tests
Tests --> Dev : ✗ FAIL (no implementation) #RED_COLOR
deactivate Tests

== Phase 3: Green - Implement to Pass Mocks ==

Dev -> Impl : 6. Implement using generated builders
activate Impl
note right #GREEN_COLOR
  fn execute_container(
    image: &str,
    span: impl ContainerExecutionSpan
  ) -> Result<()> {
    let container = create_container(image)?;

    // Use generated type-safe builder
    span.set_container_id(&container.id);
    span.set_image(image);
    span.set_state(ContainerState::Running);

    Ok(())
  }
end note

Dev -> Tests : run tests
Tests -> Impl : execute with mocks
Impl --> Tests : calls match mock expectations
Tests --> Dev : ✓ PASS (mocks satisfied) #GREEN_COLOR
deactivate Impl

note right of Tests
  Mocks prove:
  - Interface contract followed
  - Schema attributes set

  BUT: Don't prove runtime behavior!
  Need Weaver live-check next.
end note

== Phase 4: Validate - Weaver Live-Check (THE PROOF) ==

Dev -> LiveCheck : 7. weaver registry live-check &
activate LiveCheck

Dev -> Tests : run tests with OTLP export
activate Tests
Tests -> Impl : execute (real implementation)
activate Impl
Impl -> Impl : create real container
Impl -> Impl : export real telemetry
Impl --> Tests : real results
deactivate Impl
Tests --> Dev : tests pass
deactivate Tests

LiveCheck -> LiveCheck : validate telemetry\nagainst schema

alt Telemetry Matches Schema
  LiveCheck --> Dev : ✓ VALIDATION PASSED #GREEN_COLOR
  note right of LiveCheck #GREEN_COLOR
    **TRUE POSITIVE**

    Mocks proved contract.
    Live-check proves behavior.

    Feature is VALIDATED:
    - Real containers ran
    - Real telemetry exported
    - Schema contract met

    SHIP IT! ✓
  end note
else Telemetry Doesn't Match Schema
  LiveCheck --> Dev : ✗ VALIDATION FAILED #RED_COLOR
  note right of LiveCheck #RED_COLOR
    **IMPLEMENTATION BUG**

    Mocks passed (contract OK)
    Live-check failed (behavior wrong)

    Possible causes:
    - Conditional code paths
    - Error handling skips telemetry
    - Configuration issues

    FIX IMPLEMENTATION
    Re-run live-check
  end note
end

deactivate LiveCheck

== Phase 5: Refactor (With Validation Safety) ==

Dev -> Impl : 8. Refactor code
activate Impl

Dev -> Tests : re-run tests
activate Tests
Tests -> Impl : execute with mocks
Tests --> Dev : ✓ mocks still satisfied
deactivate Tests

Dev -> LiveCheck : re-run live-check
activate LiveCheck
LiveCheck --> Dev : ✓ validation still passes
deactivate LiveCheck
deactivate Impl

note over Dev, LiveCheck #2ECC71
  **Refactor Safety**

  Mocks validate interface contract.
  Live-check validates runtime behavior.

  Both must pass:
  ✓ Tests pass (mocks satisfied)
  ✓ Validation passes (behavior proven)

  Safe to ship!
end note

== The London TDD + Weaver Advantage ==

note over Dev, LiveCheck #FFEB9C
  **Traditional TDD (Classic School)**

  Red → Green → Refactor
  └─ Tests may not catch integration issues
  └─ Tests may have false positives

  **London TDD (Mock-Driven)**

  Schema → Mocks → Red → Green → Refactor
  └─ Mocks validate interface contracts
  └─ But mocks can be wrong too!

  **London TDD + Weaver (Our Approach)**

  Schema → Mocks → Red → Green → Live-Check → Refactor
  └─ Mocks validate interfaces
  └─ Live-check validates behavior
  └─ Schema is single source of truth
  └─ **NO FALSE POSITIVES** ✓

  **Why This Works:**

  1. Schema defines contract (interface)
  2. Mocks test against contract (fast)
  3. Live-check validates real behavior (proof)
  4. Both must pass to ship

  Result: Fast iteration + Real validation
end note

@enduml
